<title>UK: Texaco says N. Sea Captain field start-up delayed.</title>
<headline>Texaco says N. Sea Captain field start-up delayed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>First production from Texaco's North Sea Captain oilfield has been delayed by two or three weeks to early January, a company spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The date was pushed back after two workers died in the Spanish Bazaan shipyard where the field's floating production and storage offtake (FPSO) vessel is being built, he said.</p>
<p>The FPSO is due to leave Spain on December 10 and arrive in the North Sea on December 17, and will take two or three weeks to be fully connected.</p>
<p>The field is due to reach peak production of 60,000 barrels per day in mid-1997.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
